WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.120
The Paramount Network series "Yellowstone"&nbsp;
has, over the course of its four seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:10.480
become one of its most popular hits. So&nbsp;
fans of the series were naturally excited to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:15.360
learn that a prequel had been greenlit by the&nbsp;
network, with "Yellowstone" co-creator Taylor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.000
Sheridan serving as the sole creator this time&nbsp;
around, marking his second collaboration with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
the streaming service Paramount+, after&nbsp;
the crime drama "Mayor of Kingstown."

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.440
The show, titled "1883," follows&nbsp;
the ancestors of the Dutton family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:34.000
who are the focus of "Yellowstone," and&nbsp;
stars Sam Elliott, Billy Bob Thornton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.040
LaMonica Garrett, Tim McGraw, and Faith Hill.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:42.640
Their characters journey from Texas to Montana,&nbsp;
coming across all kinds of treacherous threats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.920
to lay claim to what would eventually become the&nbsp;
Dutton Ranch. Fans of "Yellowstone" know all too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.960
well the kinds of headaches that accompany owning&nbsp;
a piece of property that large in the modern era,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.600
and if the modern-day Duttons&nbsp;
thought they had it bad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.080
James and Margaret Dutton are about to&nbsp;
show the world how much worse it can get.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.960
There have been numerous reasons for fans to get&nbsp;
excited, from the time period to the pedigree of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:11.280
creator Taylor Sheridan. However, above all else,&nbsp;
this show has one of the most stellar casts in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:16.640
any modern-day drama, especially when it comes to&nbsp;
the casting of real-life couple McGraw and Hill.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.600
In a recent interview, McGraw&nbsp;
revealed that the cast of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.240
show could have looked quite different&nbsp;
if a certain stipulation hadn't been met.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.800
This is the one condition under which&nbsp;
McGraw agreed to star in "1883."

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.800
Tim McGraw is country music royalty,&nbsp;
with Faith Hill as his queen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.880
The two have been married since 1996&nbsp;
and have three children together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.880
so they have one of the longest-running&nbsp;
marriages in the entertainment industry, by far.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.840
While the two have shared the stage plenty&nbsp;
of times in the past, they've surprisingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.080
never acted together despite both of them&nbsp;
having rather extensive filmographies.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:54.320
In an interview with the YouTube channel DC&nbsp;
Film Girl, Tim McGraw was asked about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.240
fact that both he and his wife Faith Hill are&nbsp;
in the series, with the interviewer wondering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.920
if that was part of the stipulation for&nbsp;
him doing the show in the first place.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:07.680
McGraw replied that the end result was the same,&nbsp;
but the route was different. McGraw clarified,

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.880
"We had done a flashback scene or&nbsp;
two for 'Yellowstone's' last season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:15.600
and that was how this whole idea came about of&nbsp;
doing the prequel series. And so, once we had done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:20.400
the flashback sequence, we were sort of married&nbsp;
to each other, so to speak, as it were anyway."

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:25.200
The country music superstar added that having his&nbsp;
wife on the show was part of the deal, saying,

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.120
"[W]hen it came time to do this show, we&nbsp;
were definitely going to do it together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:34.400
period. We loved the writing so much, and there&nbsp;
was no way we were going to do it separately.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.800
But I think they were kind&nbsp;
of stuck with us anyway."

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.000
Tim McGraw and Faith Hill&nbsp;
are both country megastars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.440
so it's a big deal for them&nbsp;
to star in "1883" together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:48.320
Undoubtedly, other projects must have come along&nbsp;
over the years with various movies and TV shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:53.200
wanting the power couple to hop aboard. What&nbsp;
about "1883" was different from all of those?

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:58.400
In a separate interview with DC Film Girl, the&nbsp;
host had a chance to speak with Faith Hill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:02.560
and she asks what made her want to play Margaret&nbsp;
Dutton. Hill said that it was the writing.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.280
Taylor Sheridan does the bulk of the&nbsp;
writing on both "Yellowstone" and "1883,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.040
and he has numerous other Westerns&nbsp;
and neo-Westerns to his name.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.880
He's one of the hottest writers in Hollywood&nbsp;
right now, so it makes sense McGraw and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.960
Hill would want to hitch their wagon,&nbsp;
metaphorically speaking, to the artist.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.640
Hill goes on to elaborate,

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.120
"It's one of the best things&nbsp;
I've ever read. Truthfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:27.200
and yeah, that was really it. It was&nbsp;
the writing, the story of this family."

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.360
It'll be interesting to see how the tale of&nbsp;
James and Margaret influences the modern-day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:36.320
story of "Yellowstone." But for now, you can&nbsp;
see how McGraw and Hill's real-life relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:41.760
translates on-screen when the first season&nbsp;
of "1883" continues on Sundays on Paramount+.

